वि-√ नद् P. -नदति, to sound forth, cry out, roar, bellow, thunder, MBh.; R. &c. (with रवम् महा-स्वनम्, to roar aloud);
to roar or scream at or about (acc.), MBh.;
to fill with cries, Hariv. :
Caus. -नादयति (Pass. -नाद्यते), to cause to sound or resound, fill with noise or cries, MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to sound aloud, R.

वि-√ नम् P. Ā. -नमति, ˚ते, to bend down, bow down, stoop, MBh.; Kāv. &c.:
Caus. -नामयति, or -नमयति (ind.p. -नाम्य and -नमय्य), to bend down, incline, bend (a bow), MBh.; Hariv. ;
 (in gram.) to cerebralize or change into a cerebral letter (cf. -नामित).

2. वि-√ नश् P. -नशति, or -नश्यति (fut. -नशिष्यति or -नङ्क्ष्यति; inf. -नशितुम् or -नंष्टुम्),
to be utterly lost, perish, disappear, vanish, RV. &c. &c.;
to come to nothing, be frustrated or foiled, ib.;
to be deprived of (abl.), RV. ix, 79, 1;
to destroy, annihilate, Hariv. :
Caus. -नाशयति (aor. व्य्-अनीनशत्), to cause to be utterly lost or ruined or to disappear or vanish, RV. &c. &c. (once in Sūryas. with gen. for acc.);
to frustrate, disappoint, render ineffective (a weapon), AV.;
to suffer to be lost or ruined, Ragh. ii, 56;
 (aor.) to be lost, perish, MBh.; R.

वि-निः-√ श्वस् (cf. वि-नि-√ श्वस्) P. -श्वसिति, to breathe hard, heave a deep sigh, MBh.; R.; Kathās.;
to hiss (as a serpent), R.;
to snort (as an elephant), ib.

वि-नि-√ क्षिप् P. Ā. -क्षिपति, ˚ते, to throw or put down, infix, insert, fasten, Yājñ.; R.;
 (with मनस्) to fix the mind upon (loc.), MBh.;
to deposit, entrust with, ib.;
to charge with, appoint to (loc.), ib.

वि-नि-√ धा P. Ā. -दधाति, -धत्ते, to put or place or lay down in different places, distribute, TS.; ŚBr.;
to put off, lay down or aside, MBh.; Suśr.;
to put by, store up, VarBṛS.;
to put or place on, fix upon, direct (mind, eyes &c.), Kāv.; Rājat.;
 (with हृदि) to fix in the heart, bear in mind, Gīt.

वि-नि-√ पत् P. -पतति, to fall down, fall in or into (loc.), Hariv.; Sāh.;
to flow down, alight upon (loc.), Hariv.;
to fall upon, attack, assail, Kathās. :
Caus. -पातयति (Pass. -पात्यते), to cause to fall down, strike off (a man's head), MBh.;
to throw down, kill, destroy, annihilate, Mn.; MBh. &c.

वि-नि-√ यम् P. -यच्छति, to restrain, check, control, keep in check, regulate, Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to draw in, withdraw, MBh.;
to keep off, ib.; Kir.

वि-नि-√ युज् Ā. -युङ्क्ते (rarely P. -युनक्ति; cf. Pat. on Pāṇ. i, 3, 64),
to unyoke, disjoin, loose, detach, separate, MBh.;
to discharge (an arrow) at (loc.), R.;
to assign, commit, appoint to, charge or entrust with, destine for (dat. loc., or अर्थम्), MBh.; R. &c. (with सख्ये, to chose for a friend);
to apply, use, employ, Kāv.; Kathās.; Car.;
to eat, Dhūrtas. :
Pass. -युज्यते, to be unyoked &c.;
to fall to pieces, decay, MBh. :
Caus. -योजयति, to appoint or assign to, commit to (loc., or अर्थाय, or अ॑र्थम्), Yājñ.; Hariv. &c.;
to entrust anything (acc.) to (loc.), Mn. vii, 226;
to offer or present, anything (acc.) to (dat.), Pañcar.;
to use, employ, ŚvetUp.; Car.;
to perform, Pañcar.

वि-निर्-√ दिश् P. -दिशति, to assign, destine for (loc.), BhP.;
to point out, indicate, state, declare, designate as (two acc.), MBh.; BhP.; Suśr.;
to announce, proclaim, Yājñ.; VarBṛS.;
to determine, resolve, fix upon, MBh.

वि-निर्-√ धू (only ind.p. -धूय), to shake off, drive or blow away, scatter, R.;
to shake about, agitate, ib.;
to reject, repudiate, Vcar.

वि-निर्-√ मथ् (or मन्थ्; only ind.p. -मथ्य),
to churn out, Suśr. ;
to crush, annihilate, Kathās.

वि-निर्-√ मथ् (or मन्थ्; only ind.p. -मथ्य),
to churn out, Suśr. ;
to crush, annihilate, Kathās.

वि-नि-√ विश् Caus. -वेशयति, to cause to enter into, set down or place in, put on Hariv.; Kāv.; Rājat.;
to apply, Kāv.;
to appoint to, institute or instal in (loc.), MBh.;
to fix (the eyes or thoughts) upon (loc.), MBh.; Hariv.;
to fix or erect (a statue), Rājat.;
to establish or found (a city), Kum.;
to draw up in array (as troops), MBh.;
 (with करे) to place in tribute, make tributary, MBh.;
 (with हृदये) to impress on the heart, Rājat.

वि-नि-√ वृ Caus. -वारयति (Pass. -वार्यते), to keep or ward off, check, prevent, suppress, MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to prohibit, forbid, Rājat.;
to remove, destroy, MBh.; R. &c.;
to dismiss (a minister), depose (a king), Rājat.

वि-नि-√ वृत् Ā. -वर्तते, to turn back, return, MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to turn away, desist or cease from (abl.), ib.;
to cease, end, disappear, Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to be extinguished (as fire), Yājñ.;
to be omitted, Lāṭy. :
Caus. -वर्तयति, to cause to return, call or lead back from (abl.), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to cause to cease or desist from (abl.), R.; MārkP.;
to draw back (a missile), MBh.;
to avert, divert (the gaze), R.; Mālav.;
to give up, abandon, MBh.; R.;
to cause to cease, remove, R.;
to render ineffective, annul (a curse, fraudulent transactions &c.), ŚvetUp.; Mn.; MBh. &c.

वि-√ नी P. Ā. -नयति, ˚ते, to lead or take away, remove, avert, RV.; AV.;
to throw off, drive away, dispel, expel (a disease), Car.;
 (Ā.) to elicit, draw from (abl.), RV.;
to stir up (the Soma), RV.;
to part (the hair), GṛŚrS.;
to stretch, extend, ŚāṅkhBr.; R.;
to train, tame, guide (horses), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to educate, instruct, direct, MBh.; R. &c.;
to chastise, punish, Yājñ.; Kum.;
to induce, lead or cause to (inf.), RV. i, 1, 64, 6;
to spend, pass (time), Gīt.;
to perform, accomplish, MBh.;
 (Ā.) to pay off, restore (a debt), Pāṇ. i, 3, 36;
to expand (esp. for religious purposes), ib., Sch.;
to get rid of, give up, cease from (anger), Pāṇ. i, 3, 37 :
Desid. A. -निनीषते, to wish to get rid of or give up (egoism), ŚāṅkhŚr.

वि-√ नुद् P. Ā. -नुदति, ˚ते, to drive away or asunder, scare away, dispel, remove, RV.; ŚāṅkhŚr.;
to strike (cords), play (on a musical instrument), BhP. (v.l. वि-तुद्), Caus. -नोदयति, to drive asunder or away, dispel, Śiś.; Gīt.;
to spend (time), MBh.;
to divert, amuse, entertain, Hariv.; Kāv.; Kathās.;
to amuse one's self with, delight in (instr.), Ragh. v, 67.

(of doubtful derivation) N. of a low range of hills connecting the Northern extremities of the Western and Eastern Ghauts, and separating Hindūstān proper from the Dekhan (the Vindhya range is reckoned among the seven principal ranges of Bhārata-varṣa [see कुलगिरि, p. 294, col. 3], and according to Manu. ii, 21, forms the Southern limit of Madhya-deśa or the middle region;
according to a legend related in MBh. iii, 8782 &c., the personified Vindhya, jealous of Himālaya, demanded that the sun should revolve round him in the same way as about Meru, which the sun declining to do, the Vindhya then began to elevate himself that he might bar the progress of both sun and moon;
the gods alarmed, asked the aid of the saint Agastya, who approached the Vindhya and requested that by bending down he would afford him an easy passage to the South country, begging at the same time that he would retain a low position till his return;
this he promised to do, but Agastya never returned, and the Vindhya range consequently never attained the elevation of the Himālaya), Mn.;
MBh. &c.

वि-न्य्-√ अस् P. -अस्यति (rarely -असति), to put or place down in different places, spread out, distribute, arrange, Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to put down, deposit, place or lay on, fix in, turn or direct towards, apply to (loc.), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to mark or designate by (instr.), Megh.;
to entrust or make over to (loc.), Vikr.
